{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And he went on his journeys.</b> When he returned from Egypt to the land of Canaan, he would travel and lodge at the same way-stations where he had lodged on his way down to Egypt — this teaches you derech eretz, that a person should not change his lodging-place. Another thing: on his return he repaid his debts [for what he had taken on credit]. (Bereshit Rabbah)" "<b>From the Negev.</b> The land of Egypt is to the south of the land of Canaan."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "I read בָּאַכְסַנְיוֹת as 'way-stations/lodgings' and the final clause as 'he repaid what he had borrowed' (lit. 'he paid his debts'); the Bereshit Rabbah source attribution is placed before the final parenthetical."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:30.242455187Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}